 "director": {
  "mode": "hand",
  "notes": "One unit (the reciter joins 25-30). A palm for «تؤتي أكلها كل حين» (it leaves before «ربها»), geometric for «ويضرب الله الأمثال», wind for the uprooted tree, a mountain for «بالقول الثابت» (it leaves before «ويضل الله»). The grave's questioning, Hell (29-30) and Badr are never drawn; Al-Muyassar's battle reading (28) is not used; 28:9-12 is not glossed. «قل» (30:7): no plate. STAGING v4: c1 (25-26), the two trees as seen in this world: the same fields with date palms by day; a palm plate for it gives its fruit at every season (25:1-4, gone before «ربها»), geometric for Allah strikes parables (25:7-10). For the bad tree (26: Al-Muyassar the colocynth, As-Sa'di the colocynth and the like) nothing is drawn as a tree: a falling-leaf plate (26:4), a gust and drifting leaves for uprooted from the surface of the earth with no stability (26:6-13); the palms of the fields are not withered (the palm stands for the good tree). c2 (27) stays ambient: Allah making the believers firm in this life and the Hereafter (the questioning in the grave is never drawn) and leaving the wrongdoers astray (His acts): quiet over 27:1-4 and 27:12-18; mountain plate unchanged. c3 (28-30) stays ambient: those who exchanged Allah's favour for disbelief (Al-Muyassar reads Badr: a battle) and Hell; the Prophet's ﷺ commanded threat (30:7-12, quiet); no plate."
 },
